{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":58893,"duration_api_ms":54869,"ttft_ms":3660,"ttft_stream_ms":1110,"time_to_request_ms":190,"num_turns":17,"result":"```json\n{\n  \"agent\": \"infrastructure-engineer\",\n  \"summary\": \"No Docker and no CI/CD pipeline exist in this repo; deployment is manual via Vercel CLI/dashboard (docs/engineering/PROJECT_GUIDE.md). My scope for status-page is: making environment and version identifiers available at runtime via existing Vercel-provided env vars, ensuring the status endpoint response is never cached/CDN-served stale, and keeping it a cheap, unauthenticated, low-blast-radius check. No new infra, secrets, or pipeline changes are required unless the team wants automated CI, which does not exist today for any endpoint.\",\n  \"areas_affected\": [\n    \"Vercel environment variable configuration (read-only consumption of existing auto-injected vars)\",\n    \"Runtime/caching behavior of the new status endpoint\",\n    \"Deployment process documentation (docs/engineering/PROJECT_GUIDE.md) if a new gate/check is introduced\"\n  ],\n  \"proposed_tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"infra-1\",\n      \"description\": \"Confirm and document which environment/version signals are available without new secrets: Vercel auto-injects VERCEL_ENV ('production'|'preview'|'development') and VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA server-side at build/runtime; package.json 'version' (currently 0.1.0) is available via build-time import. No new env vars or Vercel dashboard changes are needed unless the team wants a human-readable app version distinct from package.json.\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"infrastructure-engineer\",\n      \"depends_on\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"infra-2\",\n      \"description\": \"Ensure the status endpoint route sets Cache-Control: no-store (or equivalent Next.js route segment config) so Vercel's edge/CDN never serves a stale cached health result.\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"infrastructure-engineer\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"backend-status-endpoint-task\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"infra-3\",\n      \"description\": \"Review that the 'API availability' check performed by the endpoint is cheap (e.g., a lightweight Supabase ping or existing client init check) and does not run expensive queries or leak internal infra details (connection strings, internal URLs, stack traces) in its response body.\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"infrastructure-engineer\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"backend-status-endpoint-task\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"infra-4\",\n      \"description\": \"No CI/CD pipeline exists in this repo today (no .github/workflows). If the team wants the new status-page tests run automatically rather than only via local `npm run verify`, that is a net-new CI initiative out of scope for this feature unless explicitly requested — flagging as a question rather than assuming ownership.\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"infrastructure-engineer\",\n      \"depends_on\": []\n    }\n  ],\n  \"contracts\": [\n    \"Backend status endpoint must run server-side (Route Handler, not client component) so it can read non-NEXT_PUBLIC_ env vars like VERCEL_ENV/VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA without exposing secrets to the client bundle.\",\n    \"Response body should only ever contain: availability boolean/string, version string, environment string — never raw env var dumps, connection strings, or Supabase service keys.\",\n    \"Endpoint must declare no-store caching so uptime/monitoring tools get live data, not a CDN-cached snapshot.\"\n  ],\n  \"risks\": [\n    \"If the 'API availability' check queries Supabase directly on every request, a public status page could amplify load or be used for low-effort reconnaissance/DoS probing against the database — should stay a lightweight check.\",\n    \"Exposing VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA or internal version info publicly is low-severity but is still infra-adjacent information disclosure worth a conscious decision, not a default.\",\n    \"No existing CI means a broken status endpoint could ship without automated test enforcement — relies on `npm run verify` being run manually per docs/engineering/VERIFICATION.md.\"\n  ],\n  \"tests\": [\n    \"Verify Cache-Control header on the status endpoint response is no-store (or equivalent) so the check isn't CDN-cached.\",\n    \"Verify the endpoint returns 200 with environment field matching expected values across local/preview/production without requiring new secrets to be provisioned.\"\n  ],\n  \"questions_or_unknowns\": [\n    \"Should 'backend version' be package.json's version field, the git commit SHA (VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA), or a manually bumped value? This determines whether any infra wiring beyond existing Vercel-provided vars is needed.\",\n    \"Should the status page/endpoint be publicly accessible with no auth, as implied by 'user-facing,' confirming no new access-control infra is required?\",\n    \"Does 'API availability' mean reachability of this Next.js app itself, or does it include checking downstream Supabase reachability? This affects whether infra needs to review outbound call cost/rate on every status check.\",\n    \"Is introducing a CI pipeline (GitHub Actions or similar) in scope for this feature, or is manual `npm run verify` sufficient per current team convention?\"\n  ]\n}\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"b578d961-324a-46c0-bb73-e4941f8f43ce","total_cost_usd":0.7577709,"usage":{"input_tokens":18286,"cache_creation_input_tokens":88877,"cache_read_input_tokens":306453,"output_tokens":5181,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":88877,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1850,"cache_read_input_tokens":58305,"cache_creation_input_tokens":130,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_t